# CP18 — screen 4, live case entry.
#
# POST /policy/decide prices one typed case through the live policy. A judge
# types a case and watches OURS price every option it is allowed to take: same
# legal_actions, same policy.choose, same estimator, same gates as the batch.
#
# Nothing was added to choose(). Its signature already takes everything needed,
# and p_settle(do_nothing) — shown because every EV is an uplift over it — is
# derived as p_success - uplift rather than by widening the function the batch
# depends on, or by a second estimator call that could drift from the number the
# policy actually subtracted.

settle/api/decide.py
settle/api/app.py
viewer/index.html
tests/test_decide.py
SPEC.md
PLAN.md
README.md
checkpoints/cp18.allowlist

# --- BLOCKED: two test files assert the route table is exactly three ----------
#
# SPEC §16 said three routes; CP18 makes it four and §16 is amended to match
# (A148). Two tests encode the old count and neither file is on this allowlist:
#
#   tests/test_webhook.py::test_WBH_1_the_app_declares_exactly_the_three_spec_routes
#   tests/test_viewer.py::test_VIW_6_the_mount_does_not_widen_the_api_surface
#
# Both compare app.openapi()["paths"] against a literal set of three. Both now
# see ("/policy/decide", "POST") as an extra item. Nothing else fails: the
# endpoint, the screen, and DEC-1..5 are green, and so is every other assertion
# in both files.
#
# There is no green-gate path from this allowlist. The endpoint is the
# checkpoint, so it cannot be deferred the way CP14 deferred GET /, and hiding
# it from the OpenAPI schema — mounting it as a sub-application, the trick that
# let the chart route in at CP16.1 — would be worse than the failing test: a
# first-class JSON API absent from /docs, contorted solely to satisfy an
# assertion that the spec no longer agrees with.
#
# The fix is one line in each, and both are the same edit:
#
#   -    assert declared == {
#   -        ("/webhooks/razorpay", "POST"),
#   -        ("/voice/extract", "POST"),
#   -        ("/", "GET"),
#   -    }, "SPEC §16 fixes the route table at exactly three"
#   +    assert declared == {
#   +        ("/webhooks/razorpay", "POST"),
#   +        ("/voice/extract", "POST"),
#   +        ("/policy/decide", "POST"),
#   +        ("/", "GET"),
#   +    }, "SPEC §16 fixes the route table at exactly four (A148)"
#
# Add tests/test_webhook.py and tests/test_viewer.py to a CP18.1 allowlist and
# it is two edits and a gate run.

# --- The presets needed correcting before they demonstrated anything ----------
#
# Two of the three did not do what the checkpoint claimed, and the tables looked
# perfectly fine while demonstrating nothing.
#
# `time_shiftable` has no contact verbs under §9 — its viable set is
# {do_nothing, retry, serve_notice}. So on an insufficient_funds case there was
# no message for G1 to block at 02:00 and none for G6 to suppress under a
# promise. `ambiguous` is the only class with both a retry and a message viable,
# so both presets use `do_not_honour`. The stated behaviour is what was kept;
# the case was changed until it actually showed it.
#
# The anchor moved for the same reason. 00:30 UTC put tick 0 at 06:00 IST,
# outside G1's 08:00-19:00 window, so a judge pressing Decide on the defaults
# would have met a contact blocked by the clock as their first impression of the
# gates — which reads as the demo being broken rather than as a rule working.
# 04:30 UTC is 10:00 IST at tick 0 and 02:00 IST at tick 16.

# --- One guard added for a reason worth stating -------------------------------
#
# `renderDecide` returns early when its section is missing. That is partly
# because VIW-4's DOM shim in tests/test_viewer.py knows three section ids and
# cannot be updated from here — but it is correct independently: boot renders
# four screens in sequence, and an unguarded null in the fourth blanks the whole
# page. One missing section should cost one screen.
